<p class="prntac"><b>SEPTEMBER 2026 SERVICES INDEX SUMMARIES</b></p>
<p><u><b>Services PMI</b></u><b><sup>®<br class="dnr"></sup></b>In September, the Services PMI<sup>®</sup>&nbsp;registered 54.9 percent, 0.8 percentage point above its 12-month moving average of 54.1 percent. A reading above 50 percent indicates the services sector economy is generally expanding; below 50 percent indicates it is generally contracting.</p>
<p>A Services PMI<sup>®</sup>&nbsp;above 48.1 percent, over time, generally indicates an expansion of the overall economy.&nbsp;Therefore, the September Services PMI<sup>®</sup>&nbsp;indicates the overall economy is expanding for the 76th straight month.&nbsp;Miller says, "The past relationship between the Services PMI<sup>®</sup>&nbsp;and the overall economy indicates that the Services PMI<sup>®</sup>&nbsp;for September (54.9 percent) corresponds to a 2.1-percentage point increase in real gross domestic product (GDP) on an annualized basis."</p>
